#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6dab45b-f6fd-55ec-89be-0f431180a5b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252807} {:answer/id #uuid "df8dd3ba-115f-51c1-97ce-ad9f1a812238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252808} {:answer/id #uuid "1cfd21b5-68dc-558a-9523-667aa9fae254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252809} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1bffdf-d21f-5cd8-a1ce-6bd2091d293d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252810} {:answer/id #uuid "da73b34b-f20e-593e-94ea-81cf8410b666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da73b34b-f20e-593e-94ea-81cf8410b666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252811} :answer-field/id #uuid "789dd413-fd19-5c2e-8d48-7c7725fcc86d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252806}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c14bafb6-deba-59e6-83ba-5f1bd4461fa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-105493" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{3f(x)-1}{2g(x)+2},$ determine the value of ${h}^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3f(x)-1$ and $v=2g(x)+2.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2g(x)+2)\\cdot 3{f}^{′}(x)-(3f(x)-1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)}{(2g(x)+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{f}^{′}(x)(2g(x)+2)-2{g}^{′}(x)(3f(x)-1)}{(2g(x)+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{3{f}^{′}(0)(2g(0)+2)-2{g}^{′}(0)(3f(0)-1)}{(2g(0)+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0\\cdot (2\\cdot 1+2)-2\\cdot 2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3-1)}{(2\\cdot 1+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\cdot 8}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79b19c4f-afcd-59f5-a05b-3b82e0363163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252814} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5a97e8-748e-5263-a931-6e1ae92cb731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79b19c4f-afcd-59f5-a05b-3b82e0363163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252814} :answer-field/id #uuid "c11a31b7-d8c5-5e46-9711-363f7936fd1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57f7ba5d-d0b2-5f0a-bf27-9c38b7d5be75" :question/math-academy-id "q-341011" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(4)-(\\frac{1}{2})(2)}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-1}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee2f22c-0ceb-5f3b-8f8e-ebb97c7f902c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ee2f22c-0ceb-5f3b-8f8e-ebb97c7f902c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252818} :answer-field/id #uuid "a537318f-83e9-5874-add3-56b0f3be2afe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252817}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d72eb11-db3f-5e0d-9fd0-7dd743dc99d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341028" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0} & =3{q}^{′}(0)+4{r}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =3(2)+4(-1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c090bbc8-1fc5-51ca-a64e-44459e5d75cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252821} {:answer/id #uuid "44d9749a-31f1-5939-a2e2-d94ed7d8f6f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252822} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6e3d1d-f3c8-5548-9722-375ba8f89b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252823} {:answer/id #uuid "684a73d4-8f0d-508e-9e1d-0b590a2fc205" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252824} {:answer/id #uuid "90de668c-0bc5-5468-be40-97037977efe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c090bbc8-1fc5-51ca-a64e-44459e5d75cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252821} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d6db62a-956d-58f8-a39a-b5dc6f46dfd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252820}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1eda30ce-5b87-5095-9f12-acc78818a070" :question/math-academy-id "q-48843" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(1)=8,\\,{f}^{′}(1)=6,\\,g(1)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(1)=4\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(1)g(1)-f(1){g}^{′}(1)}{{g}^{2}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907cd3df-81fe-5f32-82a1-04adc2978540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252828} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ba6b3e-671f-5020-bbe2-995377926322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252829} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7e53cc-349f-5995-9aa7-cba29e855d01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252830} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ccfb64-af42-5a0e-8d2c-b67030bad6ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252831} {:answer/id #uuid "89140d3b-6096-5b43-942b-8c763d76294f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "907cd3df-81fe-5f32-82a1-04adc2978540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252828} :answer-field/id #uuid "74eac84e-7d80-54a7-9ac7-d2f58632c75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "18e1de8e-0324-5cfc-8ed1-bb965f60a808" :question/math-academy-id "q-48965" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=-1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=-2,\\,g(2)=-5,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=1\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{5f(x)+4}{g(x)+6},$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5f(x)+4$ and $v=g(x)+6.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(g(x)+6)\\cdot 5{f}^{′}(x)-(5f(x)+4)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+6)-{g}^{′}(x)(5f(x)+4)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+6)-{g}^{′}(2)(5f(2)+4)}{(g(2)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5+6)-1\\cdot (5\\cdot (-1)+4)}{(-5+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot 1-(-1)}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
